DESCRIPTION: Arbitrary Precision Calculator (APC) is C-based application developed 
using Doubly Linked Lists to perform arithmetic operations on integers of any size 
without being limited by built-in data type constraints. The project supports addition,
subtraction, multiplication, and division for very large numbers, including negative 
operands. Each digit of a number is stored in a separate node of the doubly linked list, 
allowing efficient digit-by-digit processing similar to manual arithmetic calculations. 
The calculator also performs input validation, sign handling, comparison operations, 
and formatted result display. This project demonstrates concepts such as dynamic memory 
allocation, linked list manipulation, modular programming, and arbitrary precision 
arithmetic implementation in C.



